# LOGS' Review a Log: open is the log browser's Load A Log, whose OpenFileDialog lists the dataflash
# logs, "Log Files|*.log;*.bin;*.BIN;*.LOG", opening in lastLogDir, else the log directory
# (Log/LogBrowse.cs:269-311, 2810-2818). The owner's report of 2026-10-14: "logs tab -> 'Review a
# log' -> 'open' - doesnt do anything ... it should be a filesystem chooser". Here it is the
# window's file dialog over LOGS, its list the folder's logs (crates/mp-gui/src/file_list.rs): a
# log clicked and OK opens it in the browser, from wherever it is; the dialog opens next in that
# log's folder, and a log double-clicked there opens by itself. The box beside open still opens
# the name typed in it (log-browse.gui).
#
# Self-contained: a log directory of its own holding the healthy fixture, a telemetry log beside
# it and a folder, and a data directory holding ArduPilot's LogMessages.xml.
#
# Run as: tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/chooser-review-log.gui
env MP_LOG_DIR $WORK/logs
env MP_CONFIG_XML $WORK/config.xml
env XDG_DATA_HOME $WORK
env MP_OFFLINE 1
setup mkdir -p $WORK/logs/older && cp testdata/dataflash.bin $WORK/logs/flight.bin && cp testdata/mavlink/autotest.tlog $WORK/logs/flight.tlog
setup mkdir -p $WORK/MissionPlannerRust && cp testdata/logbrowse/LogMessagesCopter.xml $WORK/MissionPlannerRust/

screen logs
# The log browser's scripts' window, a log open in it; the dialog's fit at 1280x800 is
# chooser-loadlog.gui's, the same dialog.
window 1600x1200
budget 20
# A first budget, set by hand until a passing run records one: the log read twice, a field plotted.

expect logs.page review
expect log.open false

# open, with the box empty: the dialog, in the log directory.
click log-open
expect fly.prompt Log Files
expect fly.prompt.value ~ logs
expect chooser.id fly-prompt
expect chooser.type Log Files
# Its folders, then its dataflash logs: the telemetry log is not one LogBrowse reads.
expect chooser.files ../,older/,flight.bin
expect layout.hidden 0
click chooser-file-2
expect fly.prompt.value ~ flight.bin
click fly-prompt-ok
expect fly.prompt none
expect log.open true
expect log.fields 643

# A field plotted, then the log opened again by a double click in the dialog, which opens in the
# log's folder: opening a log clears the chart. A name of nothing first: refused, the dialog
# still asking, as the platform's does, and said on the status line.
reveal log-fields logfield-ATT.Roll
click logfield-ATT.Roll
expect log.plotted 1
click log-open
expect fly.prompt Log Files
type nothere.bin
expect fly.prompt.value ~ nothere.bin
key Return
expect status ~ there is no such file
expect fly.prompt Log Files
expect log.plotted 1
expect chooser.files ../,older/,flight.bin
doubleclick chooser-file-2
expect fly.prompt none
expect log.open true
expect log.plotted 0
